      "content": "thanks. that's a good start and definitely professional. \n\nthe problem is the sentiment score for that draft is actually pretty low—like, sitting around 0.2. our stakeholders keep pushing for these messages to feel more \"supportive\" and \"positive\" so users don't get discouraged when things go wrong with their money. \n\ncan you try another version? maybe try to bump that positivity score up a bit while still being helpful. i'm still saying don't make it weird or overly happy, but maybe find a way to make the tone feel more encouraging so the score hits at least 0.7 or 0.8? just try to make it feel a bit more \"upbeat\" about the solution.",
